diffs.patch:
Index: openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/architecture/overview.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:907d0405df61487df38e228dacc4077172ec1f5a16239a0641e1ffcd34ec3d3d",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d598e5b071174573b28ebf93b6475367",
+      "statement": "celld is an open-source daemon that runs Cloudflare Workers and Durable Objects on self-hosted machines, storing long-term state in a bucket the operator owns (S3-compatible, Google Cloud Storage, or Azure Blob Storage), with no serving control plane and no consensus service.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L3-L9",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:887fa75e09ed209146eca0eabc407bc87a0725cf4d1b886e6319a28030c00d11:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7d0f5bd8ec28441eb00bd6f9dc5a352a",
+      "statement": "The workspace comment fixes the layering rule: crates/logic owns all behavioral state and decisions and crates/celld is only an effect executor and adapter host.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://Cargo.toml#L1-L2",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:37e5549e11581997134f50a261bd592d07d9cab16474fbcecaa213c4f9e06735:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fc3c67c2a5534293aa49624ec2e92ad0",
+      "statement": "crates/ltx (celld-ltx) provides embeddable streaming replication for SQLite: it captures WAL data as LTX segments, reads and writes replica storage, restores databases, compacts levels, and reads bundle objects; the implementation is a from-scratch Rust reimplementation of Litestream v0.5.11 with the block format following LTX v0.5.2.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/ltx/src/lib.rs#L3-L9",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d36cec5113b4e81d867c113c917d7d5fc70161f83a1f0e775fec4a3bf18bbe11:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cb1a3315f7fd4c9492bb31884398ea7b",
+      "statement": "The celld crate exposes one binary target named celld located at main.rs, plus a library target at lib.rs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/Cargo.toml#L15-L24",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e7537efaab6110826257ab2ec47f46b34b2e98a3a02a625e7839ac3a1819c448:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8e08f5d45d7d4943abbac320597a4277",
+      "statement": "A cell maps to a Cloudflare Durable Object: a small server with a name and a private SQLite database that serves HTTP, holds WebSockets, sets alarms, and runs one cell on one thread with synchronous storage ops. Cell states are resident (active or idle), hibernated (retains hibernatable WebSocket clients on its node), and inactive (an object in the bucket, the state every cell starts in).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L5-L36",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac1bb776a0b640ea16dc9ee9d53d49f93856dfee8f992ac08b27b7005f458c15:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d487a4340b2c47f9a57f7d20101b0f27",
+      "statement": "Exactly one node serves a cell at a time, decided by a conditional-put ownership record; the claim expires unless renewed so a dead machine releases its cells without a failure detector, and celld does not answer a write until that write survives a failure (RPO=0).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L37-L59",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e307cea81ac921cb6f647bc93e1583bd07effd06af98ce3459117d9f644578bd:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_91c59194a796487288e9eacd8b6915b4",
+      "statement": "The celld binary main.rs doc statement: one actor serializes every event through celld-logic, polling its mailbox, timers, and in-flight effect futures together, so monotonic lease ticks can fence the node even when a storage operation hangs, without spawning a task per effect.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L3-L22",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:67db875e7906414c3fe408d169ddb1196cfafa5429b0eef8f49e24518a69ff4a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c412150f967c4bf6a1e0ceb32ad2e05f",
+      "statement": "crates/celld/lib.rs exposes the actor module as the serial lifecycle executor, with conformance test gates (conformance_core_loop_tests and multiple conformance_world_* modules) compiled only under the celld_internal_tests cfg flag, and the production actor arm separated into actor/production.rs.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L299-L435",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f8790ed19538ff73016d709bdf19a4f12cb64226c18c38e7a02f71d5b9fa9b4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0f793c1f5ac04fb8a16b603058020eb6",
+      "statement": "The node binds two listeners at startup: the public Worker listener via startup::bind_ingress_listener and an internal peer/operator listener via startup::bind_internal_listener with its own InternalListenerSettings, separate from ingress.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L3182-L3190",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc34bca8097b694fb52154f715393cc7be8ee8890e3606d6d4d194cb5adc7207:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/startup.rs#L36-L105",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36f14a0fbc26ebbcf5ec14adfd09413492ba724bbb377fd5f0e63677cfec59b1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a2fd8d782e6642edb111194521446abe",
+      "statement": "The public listener serves application ingress plus /.well-known/celld/health, which returns 200 {ok:true} only when the node is not draining, fleet-ready, and healthy, and 503 {ok:false} otherwise.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L2579-L2620",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9cd3e349532216a9e94ee2c63cd050fc6c5bb1b19530d6c1c49f27760e7e0919:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9d9512635ce5447b9490012d122694a4",
+      "statement": "The internal listener routes are peer probe/handoff/tunnel/abort/log plus operator routes: GET /state snapshot, POST /reload, POST /shutdown (with optional ?handoff=preserve selecting ShutdownMode::Preserve vs Handoff), /runtime/<scope> which serves only reserved runtime classes (rejecting plain DO scopes with 403 'use /do/ for a Durable Object'), and /do/<scope> ingress which refuses reserved scopes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L2622-L2733",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e117bba65c916eb9e73b8f863884d65e42187912d9dc2ad4970f8bb6cac92050:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ede1a761eae8417b8887c01d4266370e",
+      "statement": "Every request a node receives for a cell it does not own is proxied to the owner via signed peer HTTP transport, and node discovery of owners and peers comes from bucket leases rather than a join service.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L18-L34",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c70cfc41e5aca7e9abb4e43092bac64792a8cbd2f90c6db19f9b5d8baa4e31b0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8e2431b354614a1e8b1e45d5730e015b",
+      "statement": "A Generation is everything a node derives from a deployment — compiled Worker configurations, isolate pools, the Durable Object class registry, the service-binding graph, asset resolvers, and the cron schedule. A node serves exactly one current generation and reaches it through a snapshot, so a request started on one generation finishes on it even after the node adopts another.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/generation.rs#L7-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a846fe7149a7d8ea1ebfd9026bb6614354b5ede62e1ab8cd8ea8196a0990ab51:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2adb9062ecca43119f47fefffca5a682",
+      "statement": "A node that cannot reach the bucket cannot renew and fences itself when its published expiry passes: it stops each active cell and fails incomplete requests; the fence writes nothing to the bucket, logs SELF-FENCE:, exits code 3, and only a restart returns the node to the fleet.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/guarantees.md#L184-L205",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e81a8a1a1ea5f0354df7c90d72443831048d36094cd680530a94dfdd16f7a2dd:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:47:04.277Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/integration/peer-network-and-auth.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/integration/peer-network-and-auth.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/integration/peer-network-and-auth.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,154 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:46c9f67d0f19c66d935b4876b346039ed93371132b856a113027e7dc9d9c296d",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_8e336877f87749abbd424b6f219f43ab",
+      "statement": "Peer HTTP and the operator API use the internal listener; every advertised address must be on a trusted private network or an encrypted overlay such as WireGuard or Tailscale, the internal port is not published, and celld rejects a literal public IP unless CELLD_UNSAFE_PUBLIC_ADVERTISE is set; an explicit advertised address requires an explicit internal-listener address and routing to it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L189-L200",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bdb1590ef84c3c26ff42b4dc456dd336be8fd92935d7f08a4c470ad52a318e95:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_832109908c7e4dac8496eb25d1a5bd8a",
+      "statement": "The fleet peer-auth scheme is PEM-defined around two protocol constants: the secret key fleet/peer-auth.json at SECRET_VERSION 1 with domain cells-peer-request-v1, and the version response header x-cells-peer-version (protocol version 5: PROTOCOL_VERSION=5).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L18-L22",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:32369e2d0bf256795d42ccfd3e21bfa3835538257abe691bd7ad911c51d76ec1:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_62272b1e04f74e76a811f924ee271290",
+      "statement": "Replay protection: a signed request's timestamp must be within a 30-second clock window, a nonce is retained for twice the window (REPLAY_RETENTION_MS = CLOCK_WINDOW_MS * 2), a compile-time const assertion pins that a nonce is retained at least as long as its signature is acceptable, and the replay cache is bounded at 1,000,000 entries.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L24-L31",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:26fb4ed000e5cc3a67bec482bef8ed819b92a90068354048cbe6b91aa2ef0801:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e36bca10e005403ebaf3a569b62f3804",
+      "statement": "Signed peer requests carry x-cells-peer-source, x-cells-peer-target, x-cells-peer-timestamp, x-cells-peer-nonce, x-cells-peer-body-sha256, and x-cells-peer-signature headers; the signature is an HMAC whose canonical request binds method, path+query, body hash, source, target, timestamp, and nonce.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_auth.rs#L33-L41",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8176d9775a0a3a347de6f6d78e1318725c41fc6b72c297c1b4a659865b89a2e2:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_51f1c5da1299472785fcacc1bdeb5934",
+      "statement": "Peer discovery comes from bucket node leases, not a join service: nodes/<node>.json carries addr (where peers POST) and probe_public_key; diagnose and peer routing read these leases.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/ownership_store.rs#L27-L55",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:02bddc01c2bcc62031fd9ea5a9df9dd0569242e5455e89aa7590f3b71613df37:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_809ea040ba724ed19ea3c7be276a89fe",
+      "statement": "The signed probe is liveness and identity: a installing signer at boot, a peer GET /peer/probe with a random challenge signed by the fleet MAC, and the node responds with its advertise address and challenge signature; probe refuses a node with no signed-probe key and refuses a node whose peer protocol is not the current version.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_probe.rs#L103-L135",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e464006754200c3ccce10fbd47f71bda82fe977d24c35c3b446f3a18e5b7209b:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/peer_probe.rs#L18-L60",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3690bad01bea44de74e536c7fdf460718b26b624475f99823bc712afa3fcf5e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_265d1a867b07465ca9963f96182d3bf2",
+      "statement": "The peer tunnel is an h1 upgrade on /peer/tunnel (CONNECT mechanics with Upgrade): after 101 the connection is an opaque duplex stream and app requests cross as literal HTTP driven by hyper on both ends — the hop never interprets inner bytes so header fidelity is preserved (Host, Content-Length, Upgrade are data) — and per-call control (scope, cell name, request id, capacity handoff) rides x-cells-* inner headers that node A overwrites and node B strips so reserved names cannot be smuggled by an application.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L3-L27",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bdca9083f53efd5f7410d2e89ec7b395d5952b3e3b14067582ae0c57c79bd69a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0df151cce5f34145beeded98bb5638af",
+      "statement": "Tunnel protocol identification: TUNNEL_PROTOCOL = celld-tunnel, TUNNEL_VERSION = 5, with x-cells-tunnel-version, x-cells-tunnel-kind, x-cells-scope, x-cells-do-name, x-cells-request-id, and x-cells-capacity-handoff as the reserved inner headers.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L40-L52",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a85f07077a8e987b2014960f975b07947549b6fc603f2a35846b9297edf5c217:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a09a4e5cea0449a0adf773b7ca4d62eb",
+      "statement": "Idle tunnels are pooled per peer and reused via h1 keep-alive rather than fresh TCP per call, because without reuse a loopback-speed caller saturates the ephemeral port range into TIME_WAIT within seconds (about 1000 calls/s is the hard OS ceiling).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/peer_tunnel.rs#L22-L33",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f9c3305566f0e67a06400e9c2d022f91b92803e2508b943079a1ae828d6bc77f:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ef3297a9f23c4c2e9e62f8bced401485",
+      "statement": "The node-log tier's one peer-POST boundary is the LogTransport trait used by the log routes, and its design documents a scheduler-controlled replacement transport for the simulator, so follower entry codecs are deterministic and shared with simulation.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/node_log.rs#L52-L96",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf64daa4d203ba13e905aaf110738945e2c851755ffe9ff5d31cdc4ed3245252:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a0ece29f27374893b84d814d1268cef4",
+      "statement": "/runtime/ is the operator CLIs' way in (celld d1, kv, queue, workflows): the same forwarding dispatch /do/ uses but with the fleet authentication /do/ does not have, and it serves only reserved runtime classes, refusing a plain Durable Object scope with 403 directing the caller to /do/.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L2665-L2695",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54e3964f893296bddfdd637effb36f488c733e04b426eca1efbbb156c4f3d914:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_98cd488028004ea2b7b050a04704ab87",
+      "statement": "Operator commands reach reserved cells by finding a live node from the bucket leases, signing a request with the fleet secret, and POSTing /runtime/<scope> which forwards to the cell's owner; they cannot instead write the bucket because a bucket write happens behind the fence and the owner's next flush overwrites it, and they cannot name one node because an operator's internal listener has an ephemeral port by default.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/operator_cell.rs#L5-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ce486c74e9d05297058d27e9b66a7bacc62bbcb957fd02442b7c114170494aa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3defb77ba6c64d87a96fa6ac59bba084",
+      "statement": "Security boundary: celld is an alpha not safe for hostile multi-tenant use; one fleet runs one application and celld trusts the application code, fleet nodes, and operators; object storage credentials control the fleet and should access one fleet bucket only; the internal listener must sit on a trusted private network (encrypted overlay if not); celld does not terminate TLS, so public TLS must terminate at an ingress proxy.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/security.md#L5-L22",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7524aa17ddd1999c1c36c35c86b3293ee1b2e207c6af5522576a1b09ab3c512:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b6972930e8f84b0592f09e101c00ed5c",
+      "statement": "Peer traffic crosses the internal network as plaintext HTTP: the fleet HMAC authenticates tunnel establishment and control requests but does not encrypt application data on the wire; the network layer must provide confidentiality.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/limitations.md#L16-L21",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:054637e039dd7c9654b5927874f11110eec2ea2389d2ddc00b2084195ab6e283:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:47:04.277Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/operations/cli.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/operations/cli.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/operations/cli.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,160 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:6236a87791c7850268489076af387926b673a07c76c0b3881efb954d42fb83f6",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_50088aabd3094d02af1d827e81ed566c",
+      "statement": "The celld --help usage block is the operator command contract: run node, deploy, dev, cell list, d1 migrations apply/execute, kv get/put/delete/list/info, queue info/peek/purge/pause/resume/redrive, and diagnose, each against a fleet bucket with s3://, gs://, or az:// schemes (rejecting --endpoint and ignoring --region for gs and az).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L271-L322",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2b64001c9e2bc384556f76d7e55970bae45b317a314e04453685c023da778eab:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_424b49f67f9d46638c80228f92333584",
+      "statement": "main dispatches subcommands (deploy, dev, cell, d1, kv, queue, diagnose, connect/credentials/token) to their modules and only runs a full node when no subcommand is selected; diagnose even binds both listeners first merely as a bind check because diagnose never serves on them.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L3095-L3131",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:671fe3f4ff520a996486b38650684d902ad04cf1540a9dedac31b572b31cca21:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9f8195f08afe45f5bfe0f659234dad52",
+      "statement": "Daemon defaults: --listen defaults to 127.0.0.1:8080 (non-loopback requires --internal-listen), --internal-listen defaults to 127.0.0.1:0 letting the OS pick an available loopback port, --advertise is required for peers to reach the node, and --unsafe-public-advertise opts into a literal public advertise address with the help warning that operator routes permit unauthenticated work, eviction, state inspection, and shutdown.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L287-L322",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:31ec65b0a2cead6129332389a6b9e0f8bf18ac249dda1f0122830c64400687c7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f32493da0a184435b7d4cb6a294fcf80",
+      "statement": "celld dev runs the local development stack: one persisted local SQLite object store and one supervised celld node; only the dev command can select the local backend, and a production node or CLI subcommand cannot.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/dev.rs#L3-L30",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6beb9197d3d00181e9c1f8838d5680707fa5f90a2d270ac531ec3d0e56d77dea:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d5b63a17336d4792b95241983a050915",
+      "statement": "The dev watcher uses notify's recommended_watcher recursively watching the project directory to trigger rebuilds on source or config change.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/dev.rs#L106-L119",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f64bfdb510069f099a2eb4172efe0536c57e6baaadd259198024e34fc606e89:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0c93bb703f814f6280c5726cdaf58084",
+      "statement": "The dev display highlights the application URL and hides node warning and info logs until --logs; errors always show; NO_COLOR disables color, FORCE_COLOR forces it, and NO_COLOR takes priority.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L100-L110",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:30f97d45a1f6213f7c6d83442a57035b7f6d10d1b8f097c7a9681d314e56d7b4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d010d359570c4e959d4afe428f8472f9",
+      "statement": "celld cell list prints one Class:ID cell scope per line from the fleet bucket's ownership records, ordered by the store's key order which is what makes --after SCOPE resumable, and a repeated --after value is bailed as an error because the store resumes from a key.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/cell_cli.rs#L14-L49",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5790278b2627942332b32b58752b825e626f15165d839246ae52cd980d93e130:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_fcdf407b9dc24006861eba319180d984",
+      "statement": "The cell listing is bounded: one storage request returns at most 1000 instances so the command prints at most 1000 and reports on stderr that more exist; --all reads the whole listing.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L228-L232",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1153a987c036879e38a2ba01d2a1d2d68a6f1ed3bf14ee62d53ab692419fd872:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0be6b5220b014fde9d2aebba7e54eda9",
+      "statement": "The D1, KV, and Queue CLI commands share operator_cell.rs's reach machinery: find a live node from the bucket leases, sign with the fleet secret, and POST /runtime/<scope> for the owner to apply; they must not write the bucket directly because that writes behind the fence and the owner's next flush overwrites it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/operator_cell.rs#L5-L12",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ce486c74e9d05297058d27e9b66a7bacc62bbcb957fd02442b7c114170494aa:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_697e573410fc44889d3a8cd3147d8d15",
+      "statement": "celld queue reaches the reserved Queue cell through the authenticated fleet operator route rather than reading SQLite or implementing queue transitions itself, because the cell validates each bound and owns each mutation, so the Worker binding and the CLI cannot disagree about stored state.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/queue_cli.rs#L3-L9",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d62f3227e407c4ffc27991ba7bcd3dc757099aaae640e102986a5e4c249766eb:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_5793f967bdf74447ba83f42f23ca78c8",
+      "statement": "celld diagnose output keeps the long-standing ok/fail line shape (ok bucket ..., fail peer X: ...), writing ok/skip to stdout and fail to stderr so redirecting report.txt keeps failures visible; --json emits one JSON object per diagnostic check so the output pipes through jq.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/fleet.rs#L61-L102",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e6a08ccbd342a6a4eb3601404f89f2ca0d3fca606aff187728ffa2a7c4820638:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_afa4741dc59840f3b9f105ad567673e1",
+      "statement": "A store that cannot fence makes every peer result moot, so the diagnose probe's conditional-write rejection behaviors are provoked first and their failure takes priority over peer results.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/fleet.rs#L342-L343",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1b5dc7b55ed4d10bd353fa4fafb85fd22f151468a4b3c041a0930ac5d1c8974c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3a7edc0d05504bbcb96a60a12599d739",
+      "statement": "celld diagnose enumerates every node lease by default, performs a signed direct probe of each live peer, distinguishes expired records, malformed or unsafe advertise addresses, unreachable peers, and incompatible protocols, prints each node's resident-cell, WebSocket, RSS, CPU, file-descriptor, pressure, and shedding sample, and accepts repeated --peer NODE_ID options to restrict the check.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L204-L215",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:53445761539f2d62c90913edea33914c8f4efc46a8259e7cc6d19e3e111c959d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_005ae7e870ca4ad2966a11fcce27541b",
+      "statement": "While the node runs, GET /state on the internal listener returns the node snapshot for operators, and POST /reload and POST /shutdown (with ?handoff=preserve choosing ShutdownMode::Preserve vs Handoff) are the operator control routes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main.rs#L2635-L2647",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:946b7defc120ea0ef021278afb8ffa06eaebcb4b976260f0557af29fc74070a8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_84181b7b193a4c45bb5fd3d11d806d06",
+      "statement": "The CLI JSON stdout contract is that the subcommand's stdout is its answer — celld kv get KEY > value must write the value and nothing else, and celld d1 execute prints JSON a script parses — so stdout is kept free of whatever the process happens to warn about at startup.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/main/cli.rs#L60-L66",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:efc9737529c44b8b261d3889b7e1870a64d92cd4b899de19f13ef92a0b856dbf:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:47:04.277Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/operations/settings-and-pressure.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/operations/settings-and-pressure.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/operations/settings-and-pressure.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,144 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:fdf39377aac096751355b4b4d80e307323b39b0c4d639d60a6f9fbcd7581ab9f",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_9334eda450b54e1a91e8e83fb20329ad",
+      "statement": "The environment-variable configuration contract: an unset variable selects its documented default, a boolean variable accepts only 0 or 1, and celld exits during startup when a supplied value is invalid.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L703-L708",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:733218932d66934ef200b050d352c15c8041ed23c4da38703bb5b49109a2718e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b5f2c1059d13444d8fea043266ee69fc",
+      "statement": "Environment values are parsed and validated in two layers: machine.rs reads lease TTL, ownership-on-evict, pressure config, and local cache limits from the environment via the env_vars helpers (positive_or, flag), which also enforce the boolean 0/1 contract.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/env_vars.rs#L16-L36",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:736fb5193ecb241d9b10ca2f4b3909debffde2913192fd74ce766635588d92c0:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/machine.rs#L53-L131",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ebe56f4ab90e11c965eb34c95981b46bb2b09496763a4a0d1982c85aaede8d0a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_a7e7158c4c8a45fb80f615270eff2c3f",
+      "statement": "Isolate admission and placement are decision-core policy: admit(load, shedding) refuses placement with Refusal when the pool is at ceiling, place() and place_cell() choose placement, and PoolLimits carry per-worker and per-cell capacities.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/isolate.rs#L33-L248",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6ef68da1ae5f33e656bbb41b7c50276df3bd87691c3506e57dd20d9cfb4f3584:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e58ccba9de194c578c3734ff4425743c",
+      "statement": "Overload behavior: celld admits a maximum of 64 concurrent fetch events per Durable Object or Queue broker (CELLD_MAX_CELL_REQUESTS), returns HTTP 503 with Retry-After: 1 and X-Celld-Overload: cell without starting the excess event, emits a cell_overload_refused log event with the cell scope, node, region, in-flight count, and limit, and a fixed-rate client must count the response as rejected work so an immediate retry does not increase the offered rate.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L640-L658",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:77b4c985765e1a0b880a0b2b7937689723c054a39ef432a55f718c74a024d60b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f5e155cda5d742b19eb1926b46de5483",
+      "statement": "The pressure threshold (default 80% of available memory, set via CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB) uses the greater of the allocator-adjusted RSS and the allocator-adjusted active cgroup working set; the working set is memory.current minus inactive_file from memory.stat with measured allocator slack removed, including active kernel charges RSS does not report and excluding file and allocator pages shedding cannot return; the /state route reports all four input measurements.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L267-L282",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64b83e31d833fe1d642942f2be03ba6d43c78eb936a9bcdb6a6c521ca17d92b7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e4e938c4e3fe42f6b63bfc5a3d6dd942",
+      "statement": "memory.rs samples all four pressure inputs into Sample: rss_bytes, in_use_bytes (RSS minus allocator slack), cgroup_working_set_bytes, and cgroup_current_bytes, with resident_bytes reading RSS and cgroup_memory reading the cgroup files per platform.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/memory.rs#L14-L30",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ec62b5a3948ffa608c9f325edc2116c22cd22badb0b60e6e43ce9a0c2f6e1e6e:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b233ce8726b74e9d80b697a2f3e1a7ce",
+      "statement": "The jemalloc stats features are required by the pressure classifier: tikv-jemalloc-ctl and tikv-jemallocator with the stats feature make stats.allocated and stats.resident readable so the difference yields the pages jemalloc keeps but no cell uses (allocator slack); without it a node that shed its whole working set stays latched on an RSS number the allocator controls.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://Cargo.toml#L126-L127",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c4297e6a3071b34dd25d40598dbaf26668119a97300ad77d30a513b3d77e659b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6194e29dc67f428c9bb37fff916befd7",
+      "statement": "Two separate memory limits apply: the pressure threshold at 80% of available memory and an absolute cap at 95% of the available memory on the complete cgroup charge to protect the node when shedding cannot return a kernel charge; each limit releases at 80% of its own value so crossing one does not hold the node against the other; CELLD_MAX_RSS_MB=0 disables both, and without readable available memory the cap is 125% of an explicit threshold.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L276-L296",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9e68b9d264dcb647db273e771f54184497601626893afb962a9963d8583b406a:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d84ff1cc4e6447568bafd314aff14425",
+      "statement": "Under pressure celld durably replicates and fences the least-recently-used idle cells, publishes them as unowned without resetting their epochs, and refuses to reacquire new unowned cells; it does not shed a cell with active work or a live host WebSocket, and a spare node receives no assignment but acquires a released cell through the same bucket protocol when normal traffic reaches it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L288-L297",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63603f9b78fc89455285866655603d2700e5ee903ea9b5debb6ca8bfa4c71add:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2c6f2ee360924f89bdef646dbda89821",
+      "statement": "The pressure policy is in the decision core: PressureConfig::from_limits derives thresholds, classify() maps a Load sample and former Latches into new latches with a reason, has_headroom and resume_line supply per-metric release points, and release_target/walk_metric sequence releases; the executor never sheds a cell on its own judgment.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/logic/pressure.rs#L151-L263",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:79010d82f5aa25388c9df447fef698f9d29703a97913c4dde775e9dc9499abd5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ab160b78ccbd4a01a45b727d4adbc749",
+      "statement": "Each isolate also has a separate V8 heap limit (default 128 MB matching Cloudflare's Durable Object limit, CELLD_V8_HEAP_LIMIT_MB to change): above 90% the isolate refuses a new hibernatable WebSocket and stops a SQL result-set materialization; it serves again under 90% on both; celld measures the heap before each event and forces a collection when idle measurement is above 75% of the limit, and a process restart is not necessary.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://README.md#L297-L312",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2f338677e5a3c4257e493c66d085598d475f443f68b647b3022d4e9e983eb257:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3ac2db5a5904447dacdb4de040c673fd",
+      "statement": "Admission and pipeline knobs are documented with defaults: CELLD_MAX_LOADED_WORKERS (256), CELLD_MAX_CELL_REQUESTS (64), CELLD_MAX_RESIDENT_CELLS (hard limit at admission), CELLD_ACTIVATIONS (concurrent cold-cell activations, default min(CPU count, 128)), CELLD_LOG_CAPTURE_WORKERS (8), and CELLD_LOG_PIPELINE (4 fleet-log rounds in flight).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L686-L693",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2fed03972e8ef796503fd665d020bd8a1eb151cf711e07d49408a3d5bfdc4750:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_975ed3b69b8f465d9ecee688d18c734a",
+      "statement": "CELLD_LOG_HEDGE_MS tunes the fleet-log hedge: the default is adaptive — four times the slowest recent append, at least 250 ms and always below the eviction backstop — and a fixed value or 0 (disabling the second copy) may be set, with appends idempotent per sequence so retransmission is safe.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/README.md#L694-L695",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a3cbe4b82dd834ad99930a4b5721aa0578db198c5e0195234786326e6159e2e3:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:47:04.277Z"
+  }
+}

Index: openwiki/.claims/operations/telemetry.json
===================================================================
--- openwiki/.claims/operations/telemetry.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/operations/telemetry.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,138 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:18b16e520c7b5dd40417b9627a7c5ec2b1c793c2f0e626a962b712f14ae5ba4b",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_127924ad1b8744449f6b16fcc3e21ee8",
+      "statement": "Telemetry is off by default and the off state costs nothing; CELLD_OTEL=1 enables it.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L5-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b455dab7344baa2b49ae6e8862297cd744bc6bc10235e1af5ed0f9df5a0e5b18:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_67dd811674414ba296e15bf4a771438e",
+      "statement": "Two sinks exist: SinkChoice::Bucket writes Parquet into the operator's fleet bucket under the telemetry/traces and telemetry/logs prefixes with zero configuration beyond the flag, and the otlp sink sends to an OpenTelemetry collector instead.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L32-L33",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:64ec69093dccbd17e392ab000fdae8c445cfa9917d9315dbe750be3e915ce426:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L67-L76",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b18edba7387f5a19dbf5605b7c40006dd8b8003bddf77bb71b4edaf1dfcdf941:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f4ac4252ac80444d96169268cace1da0",
+      "statement": "Telemetry configuration: CELLD_OTEL_SINK selects the sink (default bucket), CELLD_OTEL_BUCKET can override the bucket (same endpoint and credentials), CELLD_OTEL_RETENTION defaults to 30d (none disables deletion), CELLD_OTEL_FLUSH_MS defaults to 300000 and CELLD_OTEL_FLUSH_BYTES to 5242880 (whichever limit is reached first flushes), and the standard OTEL_TRACES_SAMPLER / OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT / OTEL_SERVICE_NAME variables apply for the otlp sink.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L43-L66",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5c80857d03a0dfaf206af9b4f1710781acb66e5a63425225bf382e0a663e1e18:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_0b260011aec84a71ae924f1b8d14dead",
+      "statement": "The telemetry schema is explicitly unstable: version v0-unstable is stamped on every object so a reader knows what contract the columns follow, and column names can change before a stable release.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L38-L40",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:109799d2d9d286c3b7e416f749f6f699e7618fb4d5fc3994dc92a2d8cf498412:"
+        },
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L11-L14",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:43bc2cd0865859d2e9e19f94a61a1745addce63b4b39dfe2efaeb5cec4de85d8:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_3586063d313f4d1a98b969e16f99a55a",
+      "statement": "celld records a span for each stateless Worker request, each cell event (fetch, alarm, RPC, WebSocket message), each outbound fetch(), and each cell start, carrying request id, cell, isolate, queue wait, outbound URL and status, and durability facts; each console.log line becomes a log record carrying the trace id and span id of the writing handler so queries can join logs to traces, surviving await.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L36-L52",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:42c5ac83cdad9698ac1b302dc067a9c8912351f3e9a5ec2ec60f6162fed47c2d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e5fdc8c9669043c48733e403d2185f13",
+      "statement": "A console.log body larger than LOG_BODY_CAP (8 KiB) is truncated, because log records are telemetry rather than blob storage and one runaway line must not dominate a batch.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L38-L45",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:900f26655857289229c4951e1a13fca54a42712152dc1fac110770af243198ed:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_293f3ba7b1aa4a8f9dd0a2cdfa6f63ab",
+      "statement": "Trace interop: celld reads the W3C traceparent header on incoming requests so its spans join the upstream trace, sends traceparent on outbound fetch(), keeps a Worker call to a Durable Object in one trace, and records no metrics yet — the spans carry durations and queue waits.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L49-L54",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5865356011a464c4978e8d6be53dff590b7fa2c32fa53b0a9cd422e323f8dbca:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_f5eb6f3ff5a04ef8b60c02b8757c89a0",
+      "statement": "Internally a channel of capacity 8192 sits between the hot path and the pump: a full queue sheds (counted), and the pump drains continuously with size-triggered batching so the channel only needs to cover a scheduling hiccup rather than a full flush interval.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/telemetry.rs#L47-L49",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73a2070453b0ecae6d506616523668bc86ee0d1ee7ae729a1b0d226f02258955:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_c1dd6d0dde84467c82021ee85f067a84",
+      "statement": "Sampling: the sampler decides at request start; an unsampled request records nothing and costs almost nothing; under load telemetry sheds before requests do and celld counts what it sheds.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L54-L56",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:806f80227d453f075483312f4d4a07c76055d508b4356b4e2c7dfc00f10bfb9c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2845f5b46762489ca94779a0015885c5",
+      "statement": "Telemetry files are partitioned by node and by hour as telemetry/traces/<node>/<yyyy>/<mm>/<dd>/<hh>/<id>.parquet, so a one-day query touches only that day's files.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/telemetry.md#L96-L101",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1cb7b94669171eaa72b30d6c3bfded624b45d940f1db1f1d85e63692243355d7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_cb4643beb36e4a07b3eafd228ff341e6",
+      "statement": "The OTLP sink encodes spans and logs into protobuf request bodies via traces_request() and logs_request(), with node, region, and service resource attributes.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/otlp.rs#L166-L210",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:16e7daba80bde07de87e3d5f51ab4f9a709bd57ad2f51639f9d71cfff998d468:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
