--- openwiki/.claims/validation/testing-strategy.json	
+++ openwiki/.claims/validation/testing-strategy.json	
@@ -0,0 +1,140 @@
+{
+  "schemaVersion": 1,
+  "pageVersion": "sha256:ef343a06ef63013a637e00e791dc3fa74effb4f1246a68e4d1ca0f6d62deb808",
+  "claims": [
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ed379290dc1a4bc6af3fae543049145e",
+      "statement": "celld's testing targets its three promises: an acknowledged write is durable, a cell has one writer at a time, and code written for Cloudflare Workers and Durable Objects operates the same on celld — each promise is broken at the layer where the failure shows most clearly.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L3-L8",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:87c17137718fcdb68e29ac2bee4f122054bf255293c725c68b4fbacc63b71467:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_d222f87c202e4194afc27436d77d7287",
+      "statement": "The conformance layer runs each Workers/DO program on workerd and on celld on identical bytes with exactly equal outputs, adding fixtures for every new API surface and ported workerd/Web Platform Test suites, and before a release replays scenarios through the full celld binary in each deployment mode: storage, SQL, alarms, streams, WebSockets, and lifecycle.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L10-L33",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9fc86c8f4cb8fdc479b00f30d2802c65078a665a0ce3518561292a206be18e85:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ae97dac43f174be0bbebf79c81483309",
+      "statement": "The coordination protocol is specified in TLA+; model checking of the v0.1.0 specification found four bugs and a split-brain that lost an acknowledged write — all fixed, none surfaced by review or testing.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L44-L49",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:646efdb3a07a18ea4441728ef0d88bbf4d3a9016949b4d34864c9fdf0b214d33:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_2d4f0b3eff6d40d787346352ff3e3d0c",
+      "statement": "Most checker configurations are pinned expected failures modeled on historical bugs (or deliberately broken checkers) whose verdicts must keep producing counterexamples — a configuration that stops failing has lost its tooth; the TLA+ specs are hand-synced deliberately outside CI with a delta ledger recording what the model does not yet describe, including weaker-than-code areas.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L58-L79",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:97d2e08596096f7e74ba814b4155ab03ce25668c7850cd90149c3e117f35090b:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_e658d659f91041f7a551986107d16487",
+      "statement": "Simulating the pure decision core under adversarial schedules: latency injection, CAS races, lost responses, drifting clocks, crash at every await point, scripted cell adversaries, no V8; seeded schedulers replay failures, properties must survive tens of thousands of seeds (millions of schedule choices for core protocols); and deliberately broken protocol variants are run to prove the properties can still detect damage.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L84-L106",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a46a074e1db7fbfbfc897a9462dbe8ac211f2055cc1b29af6d90c4d687476e35:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_1f0bf1ae42c54922b74489f8a7eb1727",
+      "statement": "The live-fleet fault injection lab with real VMs and a real bucket qualifies each release: SIGKILL mid-write-stream with database deletion, freeze-unfreeze of an owner node, bucket isolation, 429-throttled bucket, and full host stop at provider level are injected between verification passes that compare durable cell state exactly across nodes (status, body, message ledger).",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L108-L145",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7ab4ab5c9dbb50db7fa629051001f7be426cc370c3b5c74c43bc9a2f8a54d1e5:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_52af167f8407474dad2953e1141365c0",
+      "statement": "Each fleet run produces an archived evidence bundle (configuration, verification sweeps, node journals, kernel logs, phase timings), and red runs are kept with the same care as green ones because a caught failure is a result rather than a retry.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L108-L112",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:aae48b89bc95d32c735ea1f2f1ba265355e80d6b267f8833250e5270ab8cbde7:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_6b368279bde646789f88bd28f29895e3",
+      "statement": "The conformance suites live in the celld crate but compile only under cfg(all(test, celld_internal_tests)) with include!(env!(CELLD_CONFORMANCE_WORLD_TESTS))-style path-driven source inclusion; a plain cargo test does not build them, so validating a decision change requires the internal-test build with CELLD_INTERNAL_* paths set.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://crates/celld/lib.rs#L299-L435",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9f8790ed19538ff73016d709bdf19a4f12cb64226c18c38e7a02f71d5b9fa9b4:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_7c96a9282364457e89b29d8edc484d5a",
+      "statement": "Lint discipline enforces the layering rule with a clippy disallowed-methods table for the execution boundary (tokio::spawn into celld::asyncrt::spawn, tokio time functions into the asyncrt equivalents, SystemTime/Instant::now into the execution-domain clocks, rand::random into labeled RNG, std::fs reads into the injected filesystem), with every disallow carrying its reason.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://clippy.toml#L1-L30",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a89bb5e485460de8d7af9d0869c82cda29024e949f8313e919010c7411a8c60:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_ae77b3ba65324840a06df9b5b6454188",
+      "statement": "The release Dockerfile's test stage depends on the build stage so breaks stop the build: it adds clippy and the sqlite3 CLI (used by the ltx fault-injection oracle), then runs cargo test and cargo clippy --all-targets --locked with -D warnings using the cache mounts.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L16-L45",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bc75eb809889327a6f3bf9a0d6a898425e3d1df7518865e2902d6a7c3a19f7d0:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_bf4779c3ef44435e99b220af5902b678",
+      "statement": "Build hygiene: the Dockerfile copies Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock and crates/ then builds with cargo build --profile release --locked, so dependency changes must update Cargo.lock; cache mounts are used for the cargo registry, git deps, and the target directory keyed by TARGETARCH.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://Dockerfile#L19-L25",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:66d2e596da71c20fd9c7756f031008141607728e789393a9e7a98c1511960f4c:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_b750e234611a43ed9c6f0541421af9cf",
+      "statement": "The release pipeline has two phases: a push to the candidate ref builds every native target, attests provenance, uploads a draft release, and smoke-builds the container; publishing the draft is a separate human-approved step after the candidate binaries pass verification, and publishing triggers the container phase building architecture images from the tagged commit into a multi-arch manifest.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://.github/workflows/release.yml#L5-L20",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfdf75807bad6980e18a2f1afc6cff784ba71c055f3fce4344a31d548d7c7b51:"
+        }
+      ]
+    },
+    {
+      "id": "claim_95919d7e7cd841249be763537d204ad4",
+      "statement": "The documented failure edge is reserve headroom: a fleet full to its resident limit cannot place a lost node's cells and degrades under multi-node failure, while a fleet with headroom succeeds; both the good restoration and the red case are measured rather than tuned away.",
+      "evidence": [
+        {
+          "resource": "repo://docs/testing.md#L160-L168",
+          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:036c8d34eb91e41a095696707d4d51bc07f22518173b74b909ead9f18a4d851d:"
+        }
+      ]
+    }
+  ],
+  "verification": {
+    "by": "openwiki/0.4.3",
+    "at": "2026-09-11T15:47:04.277Z"
+  }
+}

